            <h3 id="sec-4">4. How Do We Use Your Personal Data?</h3>
            <p>We use personal data to:</p>
            <ul><li>Create accounts</li><li>Verify identities</li><li>Verify businesses</li><li>Match employers and workers</li><li>Facilitate hiring</li><li>Process payments</li><li>Prevent fraud</li><li>Improve platform security</li><li>Provide customer support</li><li>Send important notifications</li><li>Respond to legal requests</li><li>Comply with applicable laws</li><li>Improve our products and services</li><li>Conduct analytics and research</li><li>Personalize user experience</li><li>Recommend relevant jobs or workers</li><li>Measure platform performance</li><li>Detect abuse and suspicious activity</li><li>Train and improve automated systems where appropriate and lawful</li><li>We process personal data only for legitimate business purposes and in accordance with applicable law.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-5">5. Cookies</h3>
            <h4>5.1 What are Cookies?</h4>
            <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit our Platform. They help us remember your preferences, improve your browsing experience, enhance security, and analyse Platform usage.</p>
            <h4>5.2 Types of Cookies We Use</h4>
            <p>We may use the following types of cookies:</p>
            <ul><li>Essential Cookies</li><li>These cookies are necessary for the operation of the Platform, including user authentication, security, and fraud prevention.</li><li>Functional Cookies</li><li>These cookies remember your preferences, such as language, login sessions, and display settings.</li><li>Analytics Cookies</li></ul>
            <p>These cookies help us understand how users interact with the Platform, allowing us to improve our services and user experience.</p>
            <p>Performance Cookies</p>
            <p>These cookies help us monitor Platform performance, identify technical issues, and optimize functionality.</p>
            <p>Marketing Cookies</p>
            <p>Where applicable, these cookies may be used to deliver relevant advertisements and measure the effectiveness of marketing campaigns.</p>
            <h4>5.3 Managing Cookies</h4>
            <p>Most web browsers allow you to manage or disable cookies through browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of the Platform.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-6">6. Disclosures of Your Personal Data</h3>
            <p>Kaarigar values your privacy and does not sell your personal data. We may share your information only as described below and where permitted by law.</p>
            <h4>6.1 Between Employers and Workers</h4>
            <p>To facilitate workforce matching, certain profile information may be shared between employers and workers.</p>
            <p>For example:</p>
            <p>Workers may see:</p>
            <ul><li>Employer or business name</li><li>Job location</li><li>Job description</li><li>Compensation details</li><li>Work schedule</li></ul>
            <p>Employers may see:</p>
            <ul><li>Worker name</li><li>Profile photograph (if provided)</li><li>Skills</li><li>Experience</li><li>Ratings and reviews (if available)</li><li>Verification status</li><li>Contact details, where necessary for the hiring process</li></ul>
            <h4>6.2 Service Providers</h4>
            <p>We may engage trusted third-party service providers to support our Platform, including:</p>
            <ul><li>Cloud hosting providers</li><li>Payment service providers</li><li>SMS and email service providers</li><li>Analytics providers</li><li>Customer support tools</li><li>Identity verification partners</li><li>Communication platforms</li><li>Fraud detection services</li></ul>
            <p>These service providers are contractually required to use personal data only for the services they perform on our behalf.</p>
            <h4>6.3 Legal and Regulatory Authorities</h4>
            <p>We may disclose personal data where required to:</p>
            <ul><li>Comply with applicable laws</li><li>Respond to lawful requests from government authorities</li><li>Comply with court orders</li><li>Protect our legal rights</li><li>Prevent fraud or illegal activity</li><li>Ensure the safety and security of our users or the public</li></ul>
            <h4>6.4 Business Partners</h4>
            <p>We may share limited information with business partners where necessary to provide integrated services, promotions, or strategic collaborations, subject to appropriate safeguards.</p>
            <h4>6.5 Corporate Transactions</h4>
            <p>If Kaarigar is involved in a merger, acquisition, restructuring, financing, sale of assets, or similar corporate transaction, personal data may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to applicable law.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-7">7. Your Rights in Relation to Your Personal Data</h3>
            <p>Subject to applicable law, you may have the following rights:</p>
            <ul><li>Access your personal data.</li><li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li><li>Update your profile.</li><li>Request deletion of your personal data.</li><li>Withdraw consent, where processing is based on consent.</li><li>Request information about how your personal data is processed.</li><li>Request redressal of grievances relating to your personal data.</li><li>Exercise any other rights available under applicable data protection laws.</li><li>We may require reasonable verification of your identity before processing such requests.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-8">8. Deletion of Account and Personal Data</h3>
            <p>You may request deletion of your Kaarigar account at any time through the Platform or by contacting our support team.</p>
            <p>Upon receiving a valid request:</p>
            <ul><li>Your account may be deactivated.</li><li>Personal data will be deleted or anonymized where legally permissible.</li></ul>
            <p>Certain information may be retained where required for legal, regulatory, contractual, fraud prevention, dispute resolution, tax, accounting, or audit purposes.</p>
            <p>Deletion of your account does not automatically remove information that must be retained under applicable law or legitimate business requirements.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-9">9. Transfers of Your Personal Data</h3>
            <p>Your personal data may be processed or stored on servers located within or outside India, subject to applicable law.</p>
            <p>Where personal data is transferred internationally, Kaarigar will take reasonable measures to ensure that appropriate safeguards are in place to protect your information.</p>
            <p>By using the Platform, you acknowledge that such transfers may occur where necessary for the operation of our services.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-10">10. Data Security</h3>
            <p>We implement appropriate technical, administrative, and organizational measures to safeguard personal data against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, loss, misuse, or destruction.</p>
            <p>These measures may include:</p>
            <ul><li>Encryption of data in transit and, where appropriate, at rest.</li><li>Secure authentication mechanisms.</li><li>Access controls based on business need.</li><li>Role-based permissions.</li><li>Firewall protection.</li><li>Security monitoring.</li><li>Periodic security assessments.</li><li>Employee confidentiality obligations.</li></ul>
            <p>Despite our efforts, no method of electronic transmission or storage is completely secure. Users are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of their account credentials.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-11">11. Data Retention</h3>
            <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to:</p>
            <ul><li>Provide our services.</li><li>Comply with legal and regulatory obligations.</li><li>Resolve disputes.</li><li>Enforce our agreements.</li><li>Maintain business records.</li><li>Prevent fraud and misuse.</li><li>The retention period depends on the type of data, applicable legal requirements, and legitimate business needs.</li></ul>
            <p>Once personal data is no longer required, it will be securely deleted, anonymized, or otherwise disposed of in accordance with applicable law.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-12">12. Business Transitions</h3>
            <p>In the event of:</p>
            <ul><li>A merger</li><li>Acquisition</li><li>Investment</li><li>Corporate restructuring</li><li>Sale of business</li><li>Sale of assets</li></ul>
            <p>Insolvency proceedings your personal data may be transferred to the acquiring or successor entity as part of the transaction.</p>
            <p>The successor entity will continue to protect your personal data in accordance with applicable laws and this Privacy Policy, unless you are notified otherwise.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-13">13. User Generated Content</h3>
            <p>Users may upload or publish content on the Platform, including but not limited to:</p>
            <ul><li>Profile photographs</li><li>Company logos</li><li>Job descriptions</li><li>Resumes</li><li>Certifications</li><li>Identity documents</li><li>Ratings</li><li>Reviews</li><li>Comments</li><li>Messages</li><li>You remain responsible for the content you submit.</li></ul>
            <p>You agree not to upload content that:</p>
